IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-returns`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- the financial statements a foreign company lodges with the Registrar (s 373(1)), the time in which it lodges them (s 373(3)), the additional documents of s 373(7)
-- and the unaudited alternative for a company that is dormant in Singapore (s 373(9)), as a regulative layer over the Boolean encoding in sgg-returns.l4.
-- The gates are the existing section functions, called and not restated: `s 373(3) the last day for lodging the financial statements` fixes the last day, `s 373(9) the foreign company may lodge unaudited documents in lieu of subsection (7)`
-- decides whether the dormant alternative is open, and the caller's answer from `s 365 this Division applies to the foreign company` decides whether the duties arise at all.
-- The existing DEONTIC for s 373(7) in sgg-returns.l4 is not called: the duty is written again from the text, with the clock computed from the dates instead of supplied as a number.
-- Parties are the corpus's own `Party` (sg-core.l4): the foreign company is `Foreign company`. Every period here is turned into a number of days from DATE inputs, because a TRACE has no calendar:
-- each DATE input must agree with the day of the trace on which that event happens.
-- Where the text names no consequence of its own for a missed time, the breach reason says what s 373(18) provides (the company, and every director or authorised representative who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default, guilty of an offence, fine up to $10,000).

DECLARE `foreign company accounts act` IS ONE OF
    `s 373(1) lodge the financial statements made up to the end of the last financial year`
    `s 373(1) lodge the declaration in the prescribed form verifying that the copies are true copies`
    `s 373(1) lodge the statement of the name of the auditor`
    `s 373(7)(a) lodge the duly audited statement of assets used in and liabilities arising out of operations in Singapore`
    `s 373(7)(b) lodge the duly audited profit and loss account for the last preceding financial year`
    `s 373(7)(c) lodge the statement of the name of the auditor who audited those documents`
    `s 373(9)(a) lodge the unaudited statement of assets used in and liabilities arising out of operations in Singapore`
    `s 373(9)(b) lodge the unaudited profit and loss account of operations in Singapore`

§ `Helper: the time in subsection (3) turned into days`

-- The count starts from the day of the annual general meeting where the law of the place of incorporation requires the statements to be tabled at one (subsection (3)(a), "within 60 days after the date on which its annual general meeting is held"),
-- and otherwise from the day the last financial year ended, the year to the end of which the statements are "made up" (subsection (1)); in that second case the text gives no number of days of its own (subsection (3)(b) sends the reader to the period
-- a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had), so the last day is the caller's DATE, as in the existing function `s 373(3) the last day for lodging the financial statements`.
GIVEN `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the day the last financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 373 accounts: the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` MEANS
    (`s 373(3) the last day for lodging the financial statements` `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` `the day the annual general meeting is held` `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge`)
    MINUS (IF `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` THEN `the day the annual general meeting is held` ELSE `the day the last financial year ended`)

§ `Section 373(1) and (3): lodging the financial statements, the declaration and the auditor's name`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the annual general meeting is held where the law of the place of incorporation requires the statements to be tabled at one, and otherwise the day the last financial year ended; counting="within 60 days after the date on which its annual general meeting is held" (the last day is the meeting day plus 60, from the DATE input of the meeting; the act on that day is in time) or "within such period as the directors ... would have been required to lodge its financial statements if the company were a public company incorporated under this Act which does not keep a branch register outside Singapore" (a last day supplied from outside the section)
-- FORK: s 373(1) | the statements, the declaration and the statement of the auditor's name are three lodgings, each due by the same last day ("together with"), so a missing one is a breach; the statement of the auditor's name is owed only where the statements are audited ("in the case where the financial statements are audited") | one lodging
-- FORK: s 373(3)(b) | day 0 is the day the last financial year ended, a choice of origin only: the text gives the last day by reference to other sections and not as a count from any day | the day of the annual general meeting where there is none
-- FORK: s 373(3)(a) | "within 60 days after" is read with the last day as the meeting day plus 60 (sg-periods), as the existing function does | the day before
-- FORK: s 373(1) | the duties arise only where the caller's answer from `s 365 this Division applies to the foreign company` is JUST TRUE; on NOTHING or JUST FALSE nothing is owed | a duty on every foreign company
-- Silent: the text states no time before which the statements may not be lodged, so an early lodging is not a breach.
-- src:24188 | 373.—(1) Subject to this section, a foreign company must lodge
-- src:24189 | with the Registrar, within the time specified in subsection (3),
-- src:24190 | financial statements made up to the end of its last financial year
-- src:24191 | together with a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that the
-- src:24192 | copies are true copies of the documents so required and, in the case
-- src:24193 | where the financial statements are audited, a statement of the name of
-- src:24194 | the auditor.
-- src:24235 | (3) The financial statements mentioned in subsection (1) must be
-- src:24236 | lodged —
-- src:24238 | (a) in the case where the foreign company is required by the
-- src:24239 | law for the time being in force in the place of the foreign
-- src:24240 | company’s incorporation to table the financial statements
-- src:24241 | at an annual general meeting — within 60 days after the
-- src:24242 | date on which its annual general meeting is held; or
-- src:24244 | (b) in any other case — within such period as the directors of
-- src:24245 | the foreign company would have been required to lodge its
-- src:24246 | financial statements if the company were a public company
-- src:24247 | incorporated under this Act which does not keep a branch
-- src:24248 | register outside Singapore.
-- src:24463 | (18) If default is made by a foreign company in complying with this
-- src:24464 | section, other than subsection (7A) —
-- src:24466 | (a) the company; and
-- src:24468 | (b) every director or equivalent person, and every authorised
-- src:24469 | representative of the company, who knowingly and
-- src:24470 | wilfully authorises or permits the default,
-- src:24472 | shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:24473 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000.
@ref s 373(1), (3), (18) lodging the financial statements within the time (src:24188-24473)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `this Division applies to the foreign company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements are audited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the day the last financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `foreign company accounts act`
`s 373(1) chain: the foreign company must lodge the financial statements, the declaration and the auditor's name within the time in subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `this Division applies to the foreign company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN ((PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
           MUST `s 373(1) lodge the financial statements made up to the end of the last financial year`
           WITHIN (`s 373 accounts: the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` `the day the annual general meeting is held` `the day the last financial year ended` `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge`)
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the financial statements were not lodged within the time in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)")
          RAND
          ((PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
            MUST `s 373(1) lodge the declaration in the prescribed form verifying that the copies are true copies`
            WITHIN (`s 373 accounts: the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` `the day the annual general meeting is held` `the day the last financial year ended` `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge`)
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the declaration verifying the copies was not lodged with the financial statements within the time in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)")
           RAND
           (IF `the financial statements are audited`
            THEN (PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
                  MUST `s 373(1) lodge the statement of the name of the auditor`
                  WITHIN (`s 373 accounts: the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` `the day the annual general meeting is held` `the day the last financial year ended` `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge`)
                  HENCE FULFILLED
                  LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the name of the auditor was not lodged with the audited financial statements within the time in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)")
            ELSE FULFILLED)))
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 373(7) and (9): the additional documents, or the unaudited ones where the company is dormant`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the annual general meeting is held where the law of the place of incorporation requires the statements to be tabled at one, and otherwise the day the last financial year ended; counting="within the time specified in subsection (3)" (the same last day as the financial statements above)
-- FORK: s 373(7) | the audited statement, the audited profit and loss account and the statement of the auditor's name are three lodgings, each due by the last day in subsection (3) | one lodging
-- FORK: s 373(9) | "in lieu of satisfying the requirements of subsection (7)" is read as an alternative: a dormant company that lodges both unaudited documents by the same last day owes nothing under subsection (7); the text gives subsection (9) no time of its own, so the time of subsection (3) is used; the alternative is a choice (ROR) between the two groups of lodgings | an extra duty beside subsection (7)
-- FORK: s 373(9) | the dormant alternative is open only where the existing function answers JUST TRUE; where it answers NOTHING the company has the subsection (7) group only | the alternative open to every company
-- Not encoded: the Registrar's power to extend the period for subsections (3)(b) and (7) (s 373(10), with an application and a fee, no time limit on the application), the waiver (s 373(12)), the relief orders (s 373(13), (13A)) and the Minister's exemption (s 373(17)): each is a power of the Registrar or the Minister with no time of its own in the text, and the extended time is whatever the Registrar sets.
-- src:24286 | (7) In addition to the financial statements required to be lodged with
-- src:24287 | the Registrar under subsections (1), (3) and (4), a foreign company
-- src:24288 | must lodge with the Registrar within the time specified in
-- src:24289 | subsection (3) the following:
-- src:24291 | (a) a duly audited statement showing its assets used in and
-- src:24292 | liabilities arising out of its operations in Singapore as at the
-- src:24293 | date to which its balance sheet was made up;
-- src:24295 | (b) a duly audited profit and loss account for the last preceding
-- src:24296 | financial year of the company;
-- src:24302 | (c) a statement of the name of the auditor who audited the
-- src:24303 | documents referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), or both
-- src:24304 | paragraphs (a) and (b), as the case may be.
-- src:24335 | (9) A foreign company which is dormant in Singapore may, in lieu
-- src:24336 | of satisfying the requirements of subsection (7), lodge with the
-- src:24337 | Registrar —
-- src:24339 | (a) an unaudited statement showing its assets used in and
-- src:24340 | liabilities arising out of its operations in Singapore; and
-- src:24342 | (b) an unaudited profit and loss account with respect to the
-- src:24343 | company’s operations in Singapore.
@ref s 373(7), (9) the additional documents and the dormant alternative (src:24286-24343)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `foreign company accounts act`
`s 373(7) chain: the three documents of subsection (7)` MEANS
    (PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
     MUST `s 373(7)(a) lodge the duly audited statement of assets used in and liabilities arising out of operations in Singapore`
     WITHIN `the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the duly audited statement of assets and liabilities was not lodged within the time specified in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)")
    RAND
    ((PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
      MUST `s 373(7)(b) lodge the duly audited profit and loss account for the last preceding financial year`
      WITHIN `the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging`
      HENCE FULFILLED
      LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the duly audited profit and loss account was not lodged within the time specified in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)")
     RAND
     (PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
      MUST `s 373(7)(c) lodge the statement of the name of the auditor who audited those documents`
      WITHIN `the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging`
      HENCE FULFILLED
      LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the name of the auditor was not lodged within the time specified in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)"))

GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `foreign company accounts act`
`s 373(9) chain: the two unaudited documents of subsection (9)` MEANS
    (PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
     MUST `s 373(9)(a) lodge the unaudited statement of assets used in and liabilities arising out of operations in Singapore`
     WITHIN `the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the unaudited statement of assets and liabilities was not lodged within the time specified in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)")
    RAND
    (PARTY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
     MUST `s 373(9)(b) lodge the unaudited profit and loss account of operations in Singapore`
     WITHIN `the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging`
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `Foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the unaudited profit and loss account was not lodged within the time specified in subsection (3); the company is guilty of an offence under s 373(18)")

GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `this Division applies to the foreign company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company is dormant in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the day the last financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `foreign company accounts act`
`s 373(7) chain: the foreign company must lodge the documents of subsection (7), or the unaudited ones where it is dormant, within the time in subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `this Division applies to the foreign company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF (`s 373(9) the foreign company may lodge unaudited documents in lieu of subsection (7)` `the foreign company is dormant in Singapore`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN ((`s 373(7) chain: the three documents of subsection (7)` `the name of the foreign company` (`s 373 accounts: the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` `the day the annual general meeting is held` `the day the last financial year ended` `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge`))
                ROR
                (`s 373(9) chain: the two unaudited documents of subsection (9)` `the name of the foreign company` (`s 373 accounts: the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` `the day the annual general meeting is held` `the day the last financial year ended` `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge`)))
          ELSE (`s 373(7) chain: the three documents of subsection (7)` `the name of the foreign company` (`s 373 accounts: the days from the day the count starts to the last day for lodging` `the statements are to be tabled at an annual general meeting under the law of the place of incorporation` `the day the annual general meeting is held` `the day the last financial year ended` `the last day by which a public company incorporated under this Act that keeps no branch register outside Singapore would have had to lodge`)))
    ELSE FULFILLED
